{{main|2014 Alaska gubernatorial election}}
[[Governor of Alaska|Governor]] [[Sean Parnell]] ran for another term.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.alaskadispatch.com/article/20130504/neither-democrats-nor-republicans-shocked-parnell-running-again | title=Neither Democrats nor Republicans shocked Parnell is running again | author=Pat Forgey | work=[[Alaska Dispatch]] | date=May 4, 2013 | access-date=January 19, 2014 | archive-date=March 8, 2014 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140308185010/http://www.alaskadispatch.com/article/20130504/neither-democrats-nor-republicans-shocked-parnell-running-again | url-status=dead }}</ref> Attorney and 2010 Republican primary candidate [[Bill Walker (American politician)|Bill Walker]] at first ran in the Republican primary, but withdrew and instead ran as an independent.<ref name=Walker>{{cite web|url=http://www.newsminer.com/news/politics/walker-planning-to-run-as-independent-for-alaska-governor/article_d963e46e-fafe-11e2-b481-001a4bcf6878.html|title=Walker planning to run as independent for Alaska governor|date=August 1, 2013|access-date=August 5, 2013|work=Newsminer}}</ref> Governor Parnell was defeated by Independent Bill Walker.

Former [[Mayor of Juneau]] [[Byron Mallott]] won the Democratic gubernatorial primary on August 19 with 80% of the vote.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://hosted.ap.org/dynamic/files/elections/2014/by_state/AK_Governor_0819.html?SITE=AP&SECTION=POLITICS | title = Alaska – Summary Vote Results | agency = Associated Press | date = August 20, 2014 | access-date = August 21, 2014 | archive-date = October 20, 2018 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20181020182059/http://hosted.ap.org/dynamic/files/elections/2014/by_state/AK_Governor_0819.html?SITE=AP&SECTION=POLITICS | url-status = dead }}</ref> On September 2, Walker and Mallott merged their campaigns, with Walker, who ran for governor and Mallott, who ran for lieutenant governor.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.adn.com/article/20140901/walker-mallott-join-forces-governors-race|title=Walker, Mallott to join forces in governor's race|date=September 1, 2014|access-date=September 2, 2014|work=Alaska Dispatch News|archive-date=May 6, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160506203920/http://www.adn.com/article/20140901/walker-mallott-join-forces-governors-race|url-status=dead}}</ref>

