{{main|2014 Maryland gubernatorial election}}
[[Governor of Maryland|Governor]] [[Martin O'Malley]] was term-limited in 2014.<ref>{{cite web | url =http://www.washingtonmonthly.com/magazine/may_june_2013/features/should_martin_omalley_be_presi044513.php?page=all | title =Should Martin O'Malley Be President? | author =Haley Sweetland Edwards | work =[[Washington Monthly]] | date =May 2013 | access-date =January 15, 2014 | archive-date =October 20, 2013 | archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20131020235447/http://www.washingtonmonthly.com/magazine/may_june_2013/features/should_martin_omalley_be_presi044513.php?page=all | url-status =dead }}</ref>

O'Malley endorsed [[Lieutenant Governor of Maryland|Lieutenant Governor]] [[Anthony Brown (Maryland politician)|Anthony Brown]] to succeed him.<ref>{{cite news|last=Wagner|first=John|title=O'Malley officially endorses Brown for Maryland governor|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/md-politics/omalley-officially-endorses-brown-for-maryland-governor/2013/05/11/8f4e2886-ba75-11e2-92f3-f291801936b8_story.html|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130615203604/http://articles.washingtonpost.com/2013-05-11/local/39183123_1_lieutenant-governor-candidate-marylanders-prince-george|url-status=live|archive-date=June 15, 2013|access-date=May 23, 2013|newspaper=The Washington Post|date=May 11, 2013}}</ref> Attorney General [[Douglas Gansler]]<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/md-politics/gansler-set-to-officially-launch-campaign-for-maryland-governor-in-rockville/2013/09/24/1437889e-250b-11e3-b75d-5b7f66349852_story.html | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140611144615/http://www.washingtonpost.com/local/md-politics/gansler-set-to-officially-launch-campaign-for-maryland-governor-in-rockville/2013/09/24/1437889e-250b-11e3-b75d-5b7f66349852_story.html | url-status=dead | archive-date=June 11, 2014 | title =Gansler launches his campaign for governor, pledging to shake up the status quo | author =John Wagner | newspaper =[[The Washington Post]] | date =September 24, 2013}}</ref> and [[Maryland House of Delegates|State Delegate]] [[Heather Mizeur]]<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/md-politics/mizeur-makes-her-run-for-md-governor-official-as-she-files-for-office-and-for-public-financing/2013/12/17/6e94c0e2-6767-11e3-a0b9-249bbb34602c_story.html | title =Mizeur makes her run for Maryland governor official as she files for office and for public financing | author =John Wagner | newspaper =[[The Washington Post]] | date =December 17, 2013}}</ref> sought the Democratic nomination as well.

On the Republican side, candidates had included Harford County Executive [[David R. Craig]],<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/md-politics/david-craig-unveils-del-haddaway-riccio-as-running-mate-in-md-governors-race/2013/07/16/07e67136-ee1f-11e2-bed3-b9b6fe264871_story.html | title =David Craig unveils Del. Haddaway-Riccio as running mate in Maryland governor's race | author =John Wagner | newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] | date =July 16, 2013}}</ref> Chairman of Change Maryland and former Maryland Secretary of Appointments [[Larry Hogan]],<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/md-politics/md-gop-hopeful-larry-hogan-plans-to-announce-bid-for-governor-on-jan-21/2014/01/11/06b39704-7ae6-11e3-8963-b4b654bcc9b2_story.html | title =Maryland GOP hopeful Larry Hogan plans to announce bid for governor on Jan. 21 | author =John Wagner | newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] | publisher =washingtonpost.com | date =January 11, 2014}}</ref> Delegate [[Ron George (politician)|Ron George]], former [[Charles County, Maryland|Charles County]] Republican Central Committee chairman [[Charles Lollar]],<ref>{{cite web | url=http://baltimore.cbslocal.com/2013/08/09/lollar-to-announce-run-for-md-governor/ | title =Businessman Charles Lollar To Run For Governor | publisher =cbslocal.com | date =August 9, 2013}}</ref> and 2012 U.S. Senate candidate Brian Vaeth.<ref>{{cite web | url =http://www.gazette.net/article/20131031/NEWS/131039660/vaeth-seeks-gop-nod-for-governor&template=gazette | title =Vaeth seeks GOP nod for Governor | author =Kate S. Alexander | publisher =gazette.net | date =October 31, 2013 | access-date =November 15, 2018 | archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20141102184810/http://www.gazette.net/article/20131031/NEWS/131039660/vaeth-seeks-gop-nod-for-governor%26template%3Dgazette | archive-date =November 2, 2014 | url-status =dead | df =mdy-all }}</ref>

On June 24, Brown and Hogan won their respective primaries. On November 4, Hogan was elected as governor.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/md-politics/republican-larry-hogan-wins-md-governors-race-in-stunning-upset/2014/11/05/9eb8bf46-60ac-11e4-8b9e-2ccdac31a031_story.html?tid=pm_pop |title=Republican Larry Hogan wins Maryland governor's race in stunning upset |newspaper=washingtonpost.com |access-date=November 5, 2014}}</ref>

